Strict workers may cut a Branched Session at a user entry.

The strict continuation guard still refuses every path-based session switch. A branch or
fork cut at an entry is the one explicit native transition a strict worker owns: it reuses
the durable submission publication backend, keeps the source file untouched, and takes a
fresh lease on the new file. Only the branch cut passes `allowStrictBranch`, so
`new_session` and `switch_session` stay refused for strict workers.

